      "writtenOn": "2017-12-18T19:11:37Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This is more a feature change then just a refactoring, isn\u0027t it?\n\nAnyway, two notes:\n\n1) with EAS still we should be able to prefer a LITTLE CPU, at least for non prefer_idle tasks instead here we go for an IDLE CPU and thus there are chances to wakeup an idle cluster if all LITTLEs are currently busy.\n\nIf we agree that FBT is potentially more energy efficient, cannot we move this early bail out after FBT but before computing the energy_model?\n\n2) nit-pick: the comment format is not checkpatch compliant",
