      "message": "Actually, I\u0027m also thinking that perhaps we could break here and have\n\n        if (energy_sd)\n                find_energy_efficient(energy_df, p, cpu, prev_cpu, sync)\n\nat L6794, i.e. right after this for_each_domain() and before the pre-existing mainline code which goes for select_idle_sibling or find_idlest_cpu\n\nThis will make more clear that, when we want_energy, energy awareness has priority over the performance boosting features of the mainline code, which is also clear since we force \"want_affine \u003d !want_energy \u0026\u0026 ...\" at L6756.\n\n\nIf this is a non-sense, still I think that if we should move this IF block right after the next IF (which sets sd \u003d tmp), it should be possible to break directly thus returning a valid pair of df and energy_df...",
